      "content": {
        "parts": [
          {
            "text": "I understand you want to analyze the duration of observation periods. Since \"Observation Period\" refers to a specific table in the OMOP CDM, I will proceed with constructing the SQL query. I will use 10-year age bands for stratification.\n\nHere is the BigQuery SQL query:\n",
            "thoughtSignature": "CuQHAY89a1-o6W4Q1W4pQrEPhsuilt32V5sJKFhicSo2g40p3f8n1FjD00gRTdp-Nin-hmW3LLIXh7xXyp5Xs91excdi0114EJNV1sd4dPBTzyHS-T8moXBJZOyD6tQlfeVULMRDczPy_xtGpkXuehHy_1X9UySzfLv4Yv8I5YGkjUZJAXqSOQH8BDLHUpCCL64jxYjWru1bmvJXi6lcAEcS7lGZJA0Qffgg4zRLmLtHcayWUDwWqAOzjf7m_Xdc_V45piwr5qqVCU1oMaYzcCJM7jjwvm6vs5DAvbTJ01ZK1t0j-KYQK9D8wGFEd8d7eWyOoAXzyuHPKOXIrIOCByGcdpHknF5J4_tm9fGinESs35J715HeD3M4nRCzlG1nPUe8IKWUM2EwuWwaLZrm8bJQ1PcpXTBSKEhYoviI1Ae9khPBINl7T2YnzIQbVLzSBsnVYt2yrQ1DylzpWkGVYhC5HJi2ix87bFKCi76oYd2BQVBCsgxmbvSTJuxUoEWbP-WvIEQv59zwAjFYFAVjTLz7luJdSbiJGf50rD-MEPdT3o7Tu_T1GM0eXRgGtDZK-s3EHxTx7SPDKPKIs4GIUwGFGaYpTDvOTYUSlRidfhE8v7v1EEcL6-yKZJ1NWz5_gFfJ-SD2Kw8fffIIzmwU0CBn1faIAvPNkmcDp415X2Vf2mpEZ7BRRiabHjHYb0uDMaFRvQHA6AGw1_lcDhAhe7aYMzeiTaRj1QF7DWAJeyDHX7ZHrh8dKVvKT77XGEaKNR6LybhipIZRcmv-tDzDswuzXLV8ksH8f-hkQXt6U1V-BkpmsdeLDrICdAr4TGiZSHrp5OkqwqUHyy8KIBqTYG8u3kEsI6h3gHabD1LkP4Lsco9yzysy2kHRv3Y5ZYVDa4v43ZaAxRcm73ZUk9pf4teK3-tcVBm3WHjPf4Azrp3xK0wSrxDtqS5YSpliqVyWY42h1vEUnrlo7feWZSmJd7J1s04PWltz4HtLHe1MGgI5Jm0I1pd53d0EmHbIOvI7Gsi2khU3Xo2dIGQMlBrzN4BfD5U70DUN006X_JFOxzugFWWedFNKhEVMgaZv_QH97xrkYcZ9UqnlvYMVTDyKm7LtTHtVZSkdtjC64ELLgYGH1B8lkkbiF-5usddEQPM9dhTboJ829-J7OE_tmY27R9NHB7GvuolgFWMh4PTyczbdt_c5k8n4DRst1bZ9GSXzxTdB6-FUSKbx7MuX4AHWkEA6ehOnyqaC8iZGFB7CkNEShFTWpkst_0TCwZq2T0IEamKMxXkjCGBAeWSTpAhVI2T9S-4i-wguUdkfUVqesPcgsNfCWzC8"
          },
          {
            "functionCall": {
              "id": "adk-dc6d4cae-689f-4872-b0ac-96955837dee6",
              "args": {
                "sql_query": "\nSELECT\n    CASE\n        WHEN age < 10 THEN '0-9'\n        WHEN age >= 10 AND age < 20 THEN '10-19'\n        WHEN age >= 20 AND age < 30 THEN '20-29'\n        WHEN age >= 30 AND age < 40 THEN '30-39'\n        WHEN age >= 40 AND age < 50 THEN '40-49'\n        WHEN age >= 50 AND age < 60 THEN '50-59'\n        WHEN age >= 60 AND age < 70 THEN '60-69'\n        WHEN age >= 70 AND age < 80 THEN '70-79'\n        WHEN age >= 80 AND age < 90 THEN '80-89'\n        ELSE '90+'\n    END AS age_group,\n    COUNT(duration_days) AS observation_period_count,\n    MIN(duration_days) AS min_duration_days,\n    MAX(duration_days) AS max_duration_days,\n    AVG(CAST(duration_days AS FLOAT64)) AS avg_duration_days,\n    APPROX_QUANTILES(duration_days, 100)[OFFSET(25)] AS percentile_25_duration_days,\n    APPROX_QUANTILES(duration_days, 100)[OFFSET(50)] AS median_duration_days,\n    APPROX_QUANTILES(duration_days, 100)[OFFSET(75)] AS percentile_75_duration_days\nFROM (\n    SELECT\n        p.person_id,\n        (EXTRACT(YEAR FROM op.observation_period_start_date) - p.year_of_birth) AS age,\n        DATE_DIFF(op.observation_period_end_date, op.observation_period_start_date, DAY) AS duration_days\n    FROM\n        `person` AS p\n    JOIN\n        `observation_period` AS op\n        ON p.person_id = op.person_id\n)\nGROUP BY\n    age_group\nORDER BY\n    age_group\n"
              },
              "name": "validate_omop_sql"
            }
          }
        ],
